    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0313" n="1047" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1047"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Hicks.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3,
                        1890</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 180, of the 3d
                    ultimo, stating that the minister of finance had officially communicated the
                    claim of the Hydro-graphic Commission of the Amazon to Congress, which had
                    adjourned, however, without making the necessary appropriation to pay the
                    same.</p>
                <p>The Department observes with satisfaction the progress thus made in this
                    long-pending claim, and sincerely hope that on the reassembling of Congress in
                    July next the Government of Peru may be enabled to obtain without further delay
                    the sum necessary to liquidate this just demand.</p>
                <p>You will give the matter attention in this sense at the proper time.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
